<title>USA: Alabama Power replacing Farley generators.</title>
<headline>Alabama Power replacing Farley generators.</headline>
<dateline>BIRMINGHAM, Ala. 1997-07-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alabama Power Co, a subsidiary of Southern Co said Friday it will replace all six steam generators at the two-unit Farley Nuclear Plant, located near Dothan, Alabama.</p>
<p>Southern Nuclear Operating Co, also a subsidiary of Southern Co, and the operator of the 1,720 megawatt plant, will oversee the purchase, delivery and installation of the new generators.</p>
<p>In a press release, Alabama Power said the steam generators will be supplied by Westinghouse with the first installation expected to take place in spring 2000.</p>
<p>The company did not provide terms of the deal.</p>
</text>
